<x-legal-page title="Refund and Returns Policy" description="Refund, cancellation, and returns information for purchases from Andrej Nankov.">
    <p>If something is wrong with your purchase, contact me promptly with your order or Paddle transaction reference. Your mandatory consumer rights remain unaffected.</p>

    <h2>Digital products</h2>
    <p>For immediately supplied e-books, checkout may ask for your express consent to begin digital delivery and your acknowledgement that a statutory withdrawal right can be lost once delivery begins. A refund may still be available where a file is defective, materially different from its description, or cannot be supplied.</p>

    <h2>Physical products</h2>
    <p>Where a statutory cooling-off period applies, tell me within the applicable period that you wish to cancel, then return the item unused and in resalable condition with its original components. Unless the item is faulty or the law requires otherwise, return postage is your responsibility.</p>

    <h2>Damaged, faulty, or incorrect items</h2>
    <p>Send a description and, where helpful, photographs of the issue. Depending on the circumstances and applicable law, the remedy may be repair, replacement, price reduction, or refund. Do not return an item before receiving return instructions.</p>

    <h2>How refunds are issued</h2>
    <p>Approved refunds are normally sent to the original payment method through Paddle. Banks and payment providers may need additional time to show the credit. Certain personalised goods or other legally exempt items may not be returnable unless faulty.</p>
